  dbg_dll.pcpp - Debugger compliance: a dll under its host

  Debugging a dll: breakpoints in the dll stop while a host exe that loads it
  runs. dbg_dll_host.pcpp is the host; it loads the dll from repo\bin\output
  and calls DllAdd(2, 3).

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    First build the host once:
            pcpp res\tests\dbg_dll_host.pcpp
    REPL:   pcpp res\tests\dbg_dll.pcpp -d --host output\bin\dbg_dll_host.exe
            then type each step's words
    Editor: open res\tests\dbg_dll.pcpp, F5: it asks for the host exe,
            pick output\bin\dbg_dll_host.exe
  Each step: what to type, then "->" what both front-ends show.

  Keys (REPL word = editor key):
    c = F5 (continue)   n = F10 (over)   s = F11 (into)
    finish = Shift+F11 (out)   q = Shift+F5 (stop)
    b N = click the gutter left of line N
    bt = the CALL STACK   f N = click CALL STACK row N (0 = top)
    locals = the VARIABLES pane   p X = a WATCH row for X (hover is the same)
    the program's output and keyboard = the console the REPL runs in /
    the editor's TERMINAL tab

  Steps:
   1. (start)          -> REPL: held at entry (no breakpoint)
      b 56           -> breakpoint in DllAdd (editor: before F5)
   2. c                -> stops at 56 in DllAdd (breakpoint)
      locals           -> Params: AA = 2, AB = 3;  Locals: LSum = 0
   3. n                -> 57;  p LSum -> 5
      bt               -> DllAdd at 57, then the host's frames
   4. c                -> the host prints "host got 5", the program ends
*******************************************************************************/

module dll dbg_dll;

exported routine clink DllAdd(AA: int32; AB: int32): int32;
var
  LSum: int32;
begin
  LSum := AA + AB;
  return LSum;
end;

end.
